  "query_preview": "..\n(Thursday night through Tuesday)\nIssued at 336 AM EDT Wed Oct 21 2026\n\nOn the whole, the long-term forecast period will remain uneventful. \nDry weather will persist from the weekend into at least the first \nhalf of next week. \n\nThe only feature of much interest will be a backdoor cold front that \nwill arrive Friday and provide a shot of cooler air for the weekend \nas a surface high settles across the Northeast and Mid-Atlantic. \nHigh temperatures will drop back toward the 60s/low 70s over the \nweekend with lows nudging into the lower to mid 40s for most by \nSunday. Temperatures then likely begin a gradual rebound thereafter \nas the surface high settles southward.",
